# nvcodec: NVENC API 13.0 and nvav1enc's temporal-layers
#
# Adds the property `temporal-layers` (uint, 1..3, default 1) to `nvav1enc`,
# `nvd3d11av1enc` and `nvautogpuav1enc`. With 2 or 3 the encoder writes AV1
# temporal SVC: every frame OBU carries an extension header with its
# `temporal_id`, and the frames of the upper layer are not referenced, so a
# receiver can drop them. The NVENC fields this needs,
# `NV_ENC_CONFIG_AV1::enableTemporalSVC` and `numTemporalLayers`, first appear
# in NVENC API 13.0; gst-plugins-bad 1.28.9 bundles the SDK 12.0 header.
#
# The patch therefore replaces `nvEncodeAPI.h` with the SDK 13.0 header from
# FFmpeg's nv-codec-headers, tag n13.0.19.0, commit
# e844e5b26f46bb77479f063029595293aa8f812d, `include/ffnvcodec/nvEncodeAPI.h`
# (SHA-256 4fe4094541ef0f8a13249d97a8692dc5f835a6e9dd42eeadb3e2f7321d54dc7e,
# MIT, NVIDIA's notice in the file). It differs from NVIDIA's original only
# cosmetically, as the bundled 12.0 copy does from n12.0.16.1. The file it
# replaces is CRLF upstream, so the swap is a git binary hunk: a text hunk
# would carry CRs, which the repository's patches must not.
#
# `gstnvenc.c` loads API 13.0 first and uses the header's struct versions for
# it; drivers older than 13.0 still get the 12.1..10.0 fallback with the
# struct versions GStreamer computed before. Two places stay compatible with
# them: the bit depths of AV1 and HEVC, which SDK 13.0 moved from bitfields to
# `inputBitDepth`/`outputBitDepth` (below 13.0 the old bits are written under
# their new names), and `NV_ENC_INITIALIZE_PARAMS`/`NV_ENC_RECONFIGURE_PARAMS`,
# which are 8 bytes shorter in SDK 13.0 than older drivers read (zeroed bytes
# follow both). H.264 sets its 8-bit depths explicitly under 13.0.
#
# `temporal-layers` above 1 falls back to a single layer, with a warning,
# when the loaded API is older than 13.0 (driver < 570), when the device
# reports no AV1 temporal SVC or fewer than 2 layers, or with `gop-size=0`
# (intra only); a device with fewer layers than requested gets its maximum.
# The property value itself is never changed. With temporal layers the
# encoder uses no B-frames.
#
# Applies to: gst-plugins-bad of the GStreamer monorepo 1.28.9, every target
# (nvcodec is built on Linux and Windows).
# License: LGPL-2.1-or-later for the GStreamer files, MIT for nvEncodeAPI.h
# (patches/README.md).
diff --git a/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/sys/nvcodec/gstnvav1encoder.cpp b/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/sys/nvcodec/gstnvav1encoder.cpp
